Establish an intermediate fact. Reduce the claim to the hypotheses of an applicable result. Fix the arbitrary inputs or assume the hypotheses. Establish an intermediate fact. Replace the relevant objects with their definitions.

Establish an intermediate fact. Replace the relevant objects with their definitions. Rewrite the conclusion using the stated equalities. A detailed English derivation is pending.
-/
theorem fP_inj {m : ℕ} (c : ℝ) {P Q : PX m n} (h : fP c P = fP c Q) : P = Q := by
  have h0 : P - Q = 0 := by
    apply evX_eq_zero
    intro u
    have := congrFun h u
    unfold fP at this
    have h2 := mul_right_cancel₀ (gs_ne_zero c u) this
    unfold evX at h2 ⊢
    rw [map_sub, h2, sub_self]
  exact sub_eq_zero.1 h0

/- English proof (translation)
Apply function extensionality and compare values at an arbitrary argument. Simplify using the standard rewrite rules. Expand and normalize the polynomial expressions, which then agree.
-/
theorem fP_add_smul {m : ℕ} (c : ℝ) (a : ℂ) (P Q : PX m n) : fP c (a • P + Q) = a • fP c P + fP c Q := by
  funext u
  simp only [fP, evX, map_add, MvPolynomial.smul_eval, Pi.add_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]
  ring

